# UI interaction patterns

## Icon-only actions need tooltips

Every icon-only control (toolbar, list row, archive) must have:

1. **`Tooltip`** with a short uppercase label (matches existing tooltips).
2. **`aria-label`** on the button — use `IconButton` which sets it from `label`.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — ClientsClient, PricingClient, QuotationArchive
<Tooltip label="Create revision">
  <IconButton onClick={...} label="Create revision for MH-202606-0001">
    <GitBranchPlus className="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden />
  </IconButton>
</Tooltip>

// ❌ BAD — icon button with only aria-label, no Tooltip
<button aria-label="Delete"><Trash2 /></button>
```

`Tooltip` is disabled on touch devices; `aria-label` remains required for accessibility.

## When to use what

| Control | Component |
|---------|-----------|
| Row / list icon action | `IconButton` + `Tooltip` |
| Toolbar text+icon | `Button` + `Tooltip` |
| Destructive action | confirm dialog + `hover:text-status-editing` on delete icon |

## Touch & layout

- Minimum touch target: **40×40** (`IconButton` = `h-10 w-10`).
- Stop propagation on nested row buttons (`e.stopPropagation()`).
- Modals: `ModalShell` + `useBodyScrollLock`; safe-area utilities on mobile.

## Already covered elsewhere

- Text buttons (Edit, Delete, Copy link) — no tooltip needed.
- Photo grid cells, modal backdrop dismiss — `aria-label` only.
- Segmented controls — group `aria-label` + visible segment text.

## Checklist for new UI

- [ ] Icon-only? → `Tooltip` + `IconButton`
- [ ] Toolbar icon or icon+text? → `Tooltip` + `Button`
- [ ] Delete / irreversible? → confirmation dialog
- [ ] Loading state on async actions
- [ ] Mobile: test narrow viewport and safe areas
